@@ -0,0 +1,176 @@
+# Nexus mobile = the dashboard, hosted
+
+Task 556f1c50 (2026-09-07): "update the Nexus mobile app so it is just a mobile
+view of the desktop dashboard." One canonical UI, responsive to phone size,
+consumed by the Android app.
+
+## Decision: thin native shell around the existing dashboard
+
+The app is now a single screen, `app/shell.tsx`, whose only content is a
+`WebView` showing the canonical Nexus dashboard (`TheNexus/dashboard`, Next.js)
+at the configured server URL. The dashboard itself was made phone-responsive
+in its own repo (`TheNexus/dashboard/docs/mobile-shell.md`), so every desktop
+route, control, and future change is available on the phone with no parallel
+native screen.
+
+Why a hosted dashboard rather than native parity screens:
+
+- **One UI.** The native tab set (Bridge/Tasks/Inbox/Praxis/Notes/System plus
+  Dispatch, Council, Calendar, Reports, Revenue) re-implemented a fraction of
+  the dashboard and drifted on every dashboard change. The brief rules out a
+  cosmetic parity patch.
+- **The dashboard already runs remotely.** It is served through the
+  Cloudflare tunnel at `https://nexus.vibeshiftai.com` (ingress in
+  `~/.cloudflared/config.yml`: `/api/*` and `/socket.io/*` → :4000, the rest
+  → :3000). The phone was never talking to localhost; it was already using
+  that URL for the API, with a Cloudflare Access service token.
+- **Precedent.** `TheNexus/desktop` (the Tauri travel shell) hosts the same
+  dashboard the same way and solves the same Access problem the same way.
+
+What stays native, because a browser tab cannot do it: the app identity and
+Connection settings screen (`app/settings.tsx`), SecureStore credentials,
+push-token registration and notification tap routing, the Cloudflare Access
+session exchange, Android back, safe areas, and the honest
+loading / failure / retry states.
+
+## Connectivity and session
+
+`lib/shell/session.ts` — before the WebView loads anything, the app makes one
+native `GET <serverUrl>/api/health` carrying the stored `CF-Access-Client-Id`
+/ `CF-Access-Client-Secret` headers. Access answers with a `CF_Authorization`
+cookie; React Native's Android networking stores it in the WebView's
+`CookieManager` (`ForwardingCookieHandler`), so the WebView carries the session
+on every page load, `/api/*` call, Socket.IO and SSE request. The token never
+enters web content. The same request classifies failures: `not-configured`,
+`access-denied` (login bounce, 401/403, or HTML where JSON was expected),
+`unreachable`, `server-error`.
+
+If the dashboard later bounces to `*.cloudflareaccess.com` (cookie expired),
+the shell re-exchanges the token silently, at most twice per page, then
+offers **Sign in with Cloudflare Access** — an interactive login rendered in
+the WebView, the only off-origin page it will ever show. Returning to the
+foreground re-exchanges the token after six hours.
+
+LAN/plain-HTTP URLs (e.g. `http://192.168.x.x:3000`) work the same way minus
+Access; release builds block cleartext HTTP unless the manifest allows it
+(pre-existing constraint, unchanged).
+
+## Trust boundary (`lib/shell/routes.ts`, `lib/shell/bridge.ts`)
+
+- The WebView renders only the configured origin (`classifyNavigation` →
+  `trusted`). Cloudflare Access login pages are `access-login` and are shown
+  only after the user chooses the interactive fallback. Every other http(s)
+  URL is `external` and opens in the system browser; `mailto:`/`tel:`/`sms:`
+  hand off to their apps; `javascript:`, `data:`, `intent:`, `file:`, `blob:`
+  are refused. Off-origin loads inside sub-frames are refused outright.
+- `setSupportMultipleWindows={false}`, file access off, third-party cookies
+  off, media capture granted only to the same host, `applicationNameForUserAgent`
+  = `NexusMobileShell/<version>`.
+- Bridge messages (`window.ReactNativeWebView.postMessage`) are honoured only
+  when the sending frame's URL is on the trusted origin, and only these types:
+  `ready`, `navigated`, `open-external` (http(s) only), `open-settings`,
+  `badge` (0–999), `haptic`, `reload`. Nothing else is executable from web
+  content. The injected bootstrap defines a frozen
+  `window.__NEXUS_MOBILE_SHELL__` (platform, appVersion, origin,
+  capabilities) only when `location.origin` matches, main frame only, and
+  carries no secrets.
+- Native → web navigation is a `nexus-mobile-navigate` CustomEvent whose
+  detail is a sanitized same-origin path (`sanitizeDashboardPath`: absolute
+  path, no scheme, no `//host`, no control characters).
+
+## Navigation model
+
+- `app/shell.tsx` is a singleton screen with params `path` and `n` (nonce).
+  Push taps, deep links and legacy routes all `router.navigate` to it, so the
+  stack never holds two shells; the shell applies a new `path` by dispatching
+  the navigate event into the running dashboard (client-side routing) or, if
+  the page is not up yet, by loading it.
+- `app/+native-intent.tsx` rewrites incoming `nexus://…` and http(s) links to
+  `nexus://shell?path=…` (`rewriteSystemPath`); `/settings`, `/shell`,
+  dev-client and Expo Go links pass through.
+- `app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx` no longer renders tabs: anything that still
+  navigates to `/(tabs)/inbox`, `/praxis`, … (Praxis push payloads do) is
+  forwarded to the shell with the equivalent dashboard path
+  (`dashboardPathForNativeRoute`: tasks → `/task-board`, inbox + hitlId →
+  `/inbox#<id>`, system → `/system-monitor`, dispatch → `/ops`, reports →
+  `/activity`, praxis/notes/revenue → `/`). The screen files under
+  `app/(tabs)/`, `app/task/[id].tsx`, `app/project/[id].tsx`, `app/dispatch.tsx`,
+  `app/council.tsx`, `app/calendar.tsx`, `app/reports.tsx`, `app/revenue.tsx`
+  and `components/praxis/*` are now unreachable. They were not deleted in
+  this task because a sibling session has uncommitted edits in several of
+  them; delete them once that work lands.
+- Android back walks the dashboard's own history first; when it is exhausted
+  the system gets the press. Registered only while the shell is focused, so
+  Connection settings on top keeps its own back.
+
+## Acceptance mapping (mobile side)
+
+| Criterion | Where | Proof |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Canonical dashboard UI in the app, no parallel native screens | `components/shell/dashboard-shell.tsx`, `app/shell.tsx` | `components/shell/dashboard-shell.test.tsx` "primes … then loads the requested dashboard path"; native tabs retired in `app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx` |
+| Auth / remote connectivity | `lib/shell/session.ts` | `lib/shell/session.test.ts` (headers, bounce, 401/403, 5xx, timeout) |
+| Trusted-origin bridge, no credentials exposed | `lib/shell/routes.ts`, `lib/shell/bridge.ts` | `routes.test.ts` (classifyNavigation, sanitizeDashboardPath), `bridge.test.ts` (origin-guarded global, allowlist, "carries no secrets") |
+| Push taps and deep links land on the right dashboard page | `app/_layout.tsx`, `app/+native-intent.tsx`, `app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx` | `hooks/use-notifications.test.tsx` (tap → `/shell` with `/inbox#hitl-42`), `routes.test.ts` (`rewriteSystemPath`), `tests/legacy-tabs-redirect.test.tsx` |
+| Android back, loading / failure / retry states | `dashboard-shell.tsx` | `dashboard-shell.test.tsx` (unreachable, refused token, page error, retry, sign-in fallback); back handling is device-only (see limitations) |
+
+## Known limitations (device-only or not testable here)
+
+- **Voice.** The dashboard's voice command bar uses the Web Speech API
+  (`webkitSpeechRecognition`) for wake-word and dictation; Android WebView
+  does not implement it, so those controls report "unsupported" in the
+  shell. Recording via `MediaRecorder`/`getUserMedia` and playback of chat
+  audio do work in WebView, subject to the microphone permission
+  (`RECORD_AUDIO` is declared in the manifest; the WebView grants capture to
+  the same host only). Not verified on a device in this run.
+- **Attachments.** `<input type="file">` opens the Android file/photo picker
+  in WebView. Not verified on a device in this run.
+- **Keyboard and predictive back** need a device check: with `adjustResize`
+  the WebView shrinks above the keyboard; predictive back gestures on
+  Android 14+ go through the same `hardwareBackPress` handler.
+- **Access cookie lifetime** follows the Access application's session
+  duration; the shell re-exchanges silently on bounce and every six hours
+  in the foreground.
+- **Launcher badge** requires the dashboard to post `badge`; it does when the
+  shell bridge is present (`TheNexus/dashboard/src/components/mobile-shell-bridge.tsx`).
+
+## Build artifact (2026-09-07)
+
+Built with the existing EAS preview mechanism from a clean `git worktree`
+(detached at HEAD 9dbdc58 plus only this task's files) so that unrelated
+uncommitted work in the shared checkout did not ship:
+
+```sh
+EAS_NO_VCS=1 npx eas-cli build -p android --profile preview --non-interactive --no-wait --json
+```
+
+| Field | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| Build id | `05c2e081-0837-4302-9a56-f1b8ad923916` |
+| Status | FINISHED, completed 2026-09-07T21:06:23Z |
+| App version / runtime version | 0.6.0 / 0.6.0 |
+| Android versionCode | 1 (EAS remote app version source; the same as every previous preview build, so it installs over 0.5.x) |
+| Channel / profile | preview / preview |
+| Build page | https://expo.dev/accounts/vibeshift-ai/projects/the-nexus-r7g2wx/builds/05c2e081-0837-4302-9a56-f1b8ad923916 |
+| APK | https://expo.dev/artifacts/eas/12a5NpgJzlhqGMnUO9HNDWlF2E-_OIbfx4k81ckP920.apk |
+| Local copy | `/tmp/nexus-mobile-0.6.0.apk`, 126,517,428 bytes, sha256 `b9ffe69a7b6278780e95f0b80ca10261a2814da593961aacc48fa9533238730d` |
+
+This is an internal preview build, not a store release. Because the runtime
+version changed (0.5.x to 0.6.0), an OTA update cannot deliver this change to
+the installed 0.5.0 app; the APK has to be installed.
+
+### Device-only checks still needed
+
+Nothing below could be exercised without an Android device or emulator:
+
+1. Install the APK, open the app with the tunnel URL configured, confirm the
+   dashboard renders and the Access session primes without a login page.
+2. Android back button: navigates back inside the dashboard, exits the app at
+   the root.
+3. Tap a push notification: the app opens `/inbox#<hitl id>` and the inbox
+   scrolls to that request.
+4. Open a `nexus://` deep link and an `https://nexus.vibeshiftai.com/...`
+   link from another app.
+5. Chat: send a message, watch delivery state, record and play a voice note,
+   attach a photo and a file (WebView file chooser and microphone prompt).
+6. Soft keyboard over the chat composer; predictive back gesture; rotation.
+7. Leave the app for more than the Access session lifetime and return.
